  "appliesTo": "We are required to set school term and holiday dates for maintained and voluntary-controlled schools.",
  "academyNote": "Term dates may not apply to academies, voluntary aided schools, further education and sixth form colleges in West Sussex, or to schools in the independent sector. You are advised to contact those schools direct to check on term dates as they may differ.",
  "localFacts": [
    {
      "fact": "West Sussex usually sets school term and holiday dates more than 18 months before the academic year starts.",
      "source": "https://www.westsussex.gov.uk/education-children-and-families/schools-and-colleges/school-term-dates/"
    },
    {
      "fact": "The council liaises with neighbouring authorities, headteachers, union representatives and the Diocese to align dates across the region.",
      "source": "https://www.westsussex.gov.uk/education-children-and-families/schools-and-colleges/school-term-dates/"
    },
    {
      "fact": "Term dates are based on a school year of around 195 days, and individual schools can use 5 of these days for staff training INSET days.",
      "source": "https://www.westsussex.gov.uk/education-children-and-families/schools-and-colleges/school-term-dates/"
    },
    {
      "fact": "The council publishes a 'Recommended school term and holiday dates' calendar for each year, giving the number of days in each of the six half terms.",
      "source": "https://www.westsussex.gov.uk/media/5bmdgccu/school_term_calendar_2026_27_res.pdf"
    },
    {
      "fact": "The 2027-28 calendar has 195 days split 38, 35, 29, 30, 28 and 35 across the six half terms.",
      "source": "https://www.westsussex.gov.uk/media/rm3nwxts/school_term_calendar_2027_28_res.pdf"
    },
    {
      "fact": "Term dates are only kept online for 3 years under the council's disposal policy; for older dates parents are told to contact the school.",
      "source": "https://www.westsussex.gov.uk/education-children-and-families/schools-and-colleges/school-term-dates/"
    }
  ],
